  "id": "trial-and-error-learning",
  "term": "trial-and-error learning",
  "definition": "Trial-and-error learning is the gradual acquisition of a correct association through repeated attempts, such as learning which action goes with a novel sound cue. In the source, it refers to learning pseudoword–movement links over repeated trials until the association becomes reliable.",
